[ceiling] These two square rail bearings retain the frame against vertical lift and preserve the enclosure's production sliding profile. They run in front-top's receivers and end one running fit short of the Y seam, the end the frame enters from. Each groove opens along its outer flank and Y entrance for support removal before assembly. The native combined Mark2 review in ../../enclosure/enclosure/support-bottom-gap/mark2-v2/emitted-path-review.json covers these bearings' bed-rooted supports and verifies each full-width outward X removal sweep at its supported layers; its slice predates the frame's narrowed rear, which needs a slice of its own. Release the interface contacts and cut sacrificial branch junctions before pushing a support outward. Physical removal effort, bearing finish and installed fit remain unqualified.
alternatives: A 45° corbel under each bearing would take the flat catch the frame hangs on against lift.
file: hardware/printed-parts/zone-c/funnel/funnel-frame.step
