[thin] Aft of the rails the frame narrows to pass inside back-top's two roof knuckles, one running fit off each. Beside the funnel collar's rear corner, at the brim level, that leaves 1.54 mm of wall over a patch about 4.5 mm square. The brim bearing above it stays continuous with the full-width front surround, and back-top's roof stands over it.
alternatives: A deeper roof knuckle would stand in the funnel lift-off cover's footprint. A shallower one would break its head counterbore through its own inboard wall. A thicker wall here would move the collar opening, and the funnel with it, inboard.
